# Reference gem5 MOESI timing-Ruby config for the web-search Flexus-vs-gem5
# comparison phase, mesh bring-up variant.
#
# Intent:
# - keep the same checkpoint/snapshot and simulated-machine contract as the
#   validated Crossbar reference
# - reduce the topology mismatch against Flexus BuildMesh
# - change topology knobs only; keep restore and machine geometry stable
#
# Current assumption:
# - Flexus records BuildMesh but does not record mesh dimensions in the checked
#   config files we use here
# - this first gem5 mesh variant uses an 8-router 2x4 mesh via mesh_rows=2
# - if later evidence shows a different intended mesh shape, update this file
#   and rerun the reference
#
# Current known non-equivalence that remains outside this file:
# - Flexus LLC slice homing uses 4KB group interleaving; current gem5 Ruby
#   still cannot express that homing rule faithfully.

# Cache geometry aligned to the recorded Flexus machine.
--l1i_size=64kB
--l1i_assoc=8
--l1d_size=64kB
--l1d_assoc=8
--l2_size=1MB
--l2_assoc=16
--num-l2caches=8
--num-dirs=8
--topology=Mesh_XY
--mesh-rows=2

# Memory geometry aligned to the current web-search experiment.
--mem-type=DDR4_2400_8x8
--mem-channels=1
--mem-ranks=4

# MMU geometry aligned to the recorded Flexus machine contract.
--itb-size=64
--dtb-size=64
--have-large-asid-64

# Warm restored frontend/MMU state.
--restore-btb-state
--restore-tage-state
--restore-tlb-state

# Core/frontend geometry aligned to timing.cfg where the current gem5 path has
# direct knobs.
--fdip
--ftqSize=8
--btb-entries=16384
--btb-ways=4
--fetch-width=8
--decode-width=8
--rename-width=8
--dispatch-width=8
--issue-width=8
--wb-width=8
--commit-width=4
--fetch-queue-size=48
--rob-entries=140
--sq-entries=12
